      "currency": "USD",
      "description": "AGAIN. is the rehearsal app that remembers why the band stopped.\n\nYou run the tune. Somebody stops it. \"Bass, you're early on the bridge — verse two is four bars, not eight.\" Everyone nods. Next week nobody remembers. AGAIN. does.\n\nPUT THE PHONE WHERE IT CAN HEAR THE ROOM\nTap Record and play. Tell the band you're recording. AGAIN. keeps going with the screen off, as long as the rehearsal runs. Or import a recording you already made.\n\nIT FINDS EVERY STOP\nOn-device sound analysis tells music from talking. Each time the band stops to talk, that stop becomes a rehearsal letter — A, B, C — like the boxed letters in a score.\n\nIT WRITES THE NOTES\nWhat was said after each stop is transcribed on your iPhone and turned into short notes: who it's for, which song, what kind of fix (tempo, entrance, ending, arrangement, dynamics, sound, pitch, lyrics). Wrong? Edit any note, or write your own.\n\n▶ THE 15 SECONDS BEFORE\nEvery stop and every note has a play button that plays the music right before the band stopped. No scrubbing. Everyone hears the spot.\n\nMORE THAN ONE BAND, MORE THAN ONE SETLIST\nPlay in a band, a choir and a trio? Tap the band's name to switch. Each band keeps its own players, setlists, rehearsals and notes. Give a band as many setlists as it needs (Sunday service, the wedding, the club set) and pick one before you record: its songs are the ones you tap while you play.\n\nBY SONG, BY PLAYER, BY WORD\nSongs: every note on each tune, across rehearsals. Players: each musician's list, ready to send. Search: notes and full transcripts.\n\nYOURS, ON YOUR PHONE\nNo account. No ads. No servers. Recordings, transcripts and notes stay on your iPhone. Speech recognition and note-writing run on device.\n\nAGAIN. records other people's voices. Always tell the room you're recording and follow the recording laws where you play.",
